From: CEB-GNRD maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] network: count a routable NC-SI link toward online state

ActivationPolicy=manual otherwise defaults to RequiredForOnline=no. With
eth0 unplugged this leaves the machine offline even when eth1 is routable,
so timesyncd refuses to connect. Preserve the POST gate while explicitly
including enabled eth1 in online detection. Disabled eth1 remains optional.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD board policy]

--- a/src/ethernet_interface.cpp
+++ b/src/ethernet_interface.cpp
@@ -970,6 +970,11 @@
             // precedence over the board fallback 10-bmc-eth1-ncsi.network.
             link["ActivationPolicy"].emplace_back("manual");
         }
+        if (interfaceName() == "eth1")
+        {
+            link["RequiredForOnline"].emplace_back(
+                EthernetInterfaceIntf::nicEnabled() ? "routable" : "no");
+        }
     }
     {
         auto& network = config.map["Network"].emplace_back();
